## High-Level Technical Design

**Constraint classes (geometric asymmetry):**

```mermaid
graph TD
  subgraph Water phase (fine, R_w)
    W[water particles] -- PBF density rho0*(1-as) --> W
  end
  subgraph Sand phase (coarse, R_s)
    S[grain particles] -- rigid XPBD contact + friction --> S
  end
  W -. "porosity field a_s (kernel h_c)" .-> S
  S -. "a_s modulates water density target" .-> W
  W == "Darcy drag (exponential), pressure-gradient buoyancy" ==> S
  S == "equal+opposite drag/buoyancy impulse" ==> W
  X[NO water-sand sphere collision]:::x
  classDef x fill:#511,stroke:#a33,color:#fff
```

Dotted = volumetric field coupling; double = momentum (drag + buoyancy) coupling; the red node is the removed mechanism.

**Per-substep pass order (current → changed). Bold = changed.**

```
predict
water density loop (×water_iters):
    [regrid + reorder every k]
    compute_fractions        → a_s over h_c           (KTD-5: wider kernel)
    compute_boundary (solids)
    compute_lambda           → uses rho0*(1-a_s)       (unchanged)
    compute_dp
    **(REMOVED) exclude_water / exclude_grain**        (KTD-2)
    apply_dp                 → **grain dp=0 here**     (KTD-2 fix)
drag subiters (×drag_subiters):
    compute_coupling_scale   → **Darcy beta / tau_s into coupling_scale** (KTD-3,5)
    vel→vel_frozen
    drag_water / drag_grain  → **exponential Δv, momentum-conserving**    (KTD-3,4)
    apply_drag_pred
buoyancy:                    → **kept separate, re-validated**            (KTD-7)
bed contact loop (×bed_iters): bed_project + apply_dp   (unchanged — sand-sand)
finalize                     → **sleep/wake reconciled with strong drag** (R5)
xsph (water)                 (watch fine-resolution normalization)
wetting / extraction / fines (unchanged scalar layers)
```

**Exponential drag (directional pseudo-code, not spec):**

```
# per grain i, gathered over water neighbors j within h_c (and mirror on water side)
eps   = clamp(1 - alpha_s[i], 0.35, 0.999)          # local porosity
beta  = 150 * mu * (1-eps)^2 / (eps^3 * d^2)         # Darcy/K-C, reduced units
tau   = m_eff_i / (beta * V_i)                        # stopping time
alpha = 1 - exp(-dt / tau)                            # exponential factor, in [0,1)
# symmetric, opposite-mass split over the relative velocity (momentum-conserving):
dv_i  = alpha * (m_j/(m_i+m_j)) * (vel_frozen[j] - vel_frozen[i])    # summed over j
```

